Problem: Set up AWS CloudTrail for Monitoring API Calls
Tasks to be Performed
1. Open CloudTrail from Console.
2. Create a Trail & Apply to all regions.
3. Create a new S3 bucket for log storage.
4. Perform an AWS action (e.g., stop/start EC2).
5. Check if CloudTrail logs the action.

1. Login to AWS Console
Open
AWS Console
Login to your AWS account.
2. Open CloudTrail Service

In top search bar type:

CloudTrail
Open
AWS CloudTrail
3. Create a Trail
Open Trails
Left sidebar → Trails

Click:

Create trail
4. Configure Trail
Trail Name

Enter:

MyTrail
Apply Trail to All Regions

Under:

Choose log events

Select:

Enable for all regions
5. Create S3 Bucket for Logs
Storage Location

Under:

Storage location

Choose:

Create new S3 bucket
Bucket Name

Enter unique bucket name.

Example:

cloudtrail-logs-sahil123
6. Keep Default Settings

Do not change other settings.

7. Create Trail

Click:

Create trail

CloudTrail setup completed.

8. Perform an AWS Action

Now perform any AWS action so CloudTrail can log it.

Example:

Stop EC2 instance
Start EC2 instance
9. Open EC2

Search:

EC2
Open
Amazon Elastic Compute Cloud
10. Stop or Start an Instance
Open Instances
Left sidebar → Instances
Select an EC2 instance
Perform Action

Click:

Instance state

Choose either:

Stop instance

OR

Start instance

Action performed successfully.

11. Verify CloudTrail Logs
Open CloudTrail

Search:

CloudTrail
Open Event History
Left sidebar → Event history
12. Check Logged Action

You will see events like:

StartInstances
StopInstances
Verify Details

Click event name.

You can view:

Username
Time of action
EC2 instance ID
API event name
Source IP address
13. Verify Logs in S3 Bucket (Optional)
Open S3

Search:

S3
Open created CloudTrail bucket

Example:

cloudtrail-logs-sahil123
Open Log Files

Navigate folders:

AWSLogs → Account-ID → CloudTrail

You will see CloudTrail log files stored automatically.
